bin
# The built CLI binaries, not the package directory. A bare "hub" also matched
# cmd/soloz/, so every new source file added there was silently ignored — the file
# stays untracked, the build keeps working locally, and the change is lost.
/hub
/cmd/soloz/soloz
hub.exe
codebase.md
.kiro/specs/agentic-enterprise-onboarding/references
docs/metrics
kubeconfig.zero-ops/
.env
fixes
# Helm charts cached by local kustomize --enable-helm builds (ArgoCD fetches them itself)
manifests/spoke/**/charts/
manifests/hub-core-services/**/charts/
# Hybrid home-lab environment (contains real IPs/hostnames - do not commit)
scripts/hybrid/home-lab.env
scripts/hybrid/home-lab.env.bak-*
reference-projects
.zero-ops/*.log
.zero-ops/*.out
# Node build output, ignored repo-wide rather than per package.
#
# This was one line naming packages/kratos-ui, added after that package's
# node_modules and dist showed up in a diff. Naming a package only holds until
# the next one is added without its own .gitignore, and the symptom then is tens
# of thousands of files appearing in a status the author has to notice and undo
# by hand. Only packages/auth carries its own today.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Bootstrap runtime state — machine-local, never source of truth.
#
# infisical-bootstrap.json holds a LIVE machine-identity clientSecret. It is not a
# generated GitOps artifact (those live under manifests/**/generated/ and are
# committed on purpose); publishing it would leak a working credential.
.zero-ops/infisical-bootstrap.json

# Compiled Go binaries.
#
# 24 of these reached history before this rule existed — roughly 969MB across
# eight paths, every one a macOS build from a laptop. They arrive the same way
# each time: `go build` writes next to the source unless told otherwise, and a
# later `git add -A` sweeps the result in. `cmd/soloz/soloz` is what `go build`
# produces run from inside that directory; `main` is what it produces with no
# -o flag at all.
#
# ROOT-LEVEL entries are anchored with a leading slash, because these share a
# name with source directories (cmd/kube-sbt, internal/kube-sbt). A bare
# `kube-sbt` would match at any depth and hide the package tree — the tree would
# look clean while source changes went uncommitted, which is worse than the
# problem being solved. That mistake was made here once already.
/kube-sbt
/hub
/mcp-server
/auth-proxy
/main
/cnpg2monitor
/zero-ops
/zero-ops-api

# Built INSIDE their own package directory, so they cannot be anchored to the
# root. Named in full for the same reason: a bare `hub` would also ignore any
# directory called hub.
cmd/soloz/soloz
cmd/mcp-server/mcp-server
cmd/auth-proxy/auth-proxy
cmd/kube-sbt/kube-sbt

# bin/ was already ignored, but bin/zero-ops-api was committed before that rule
# and stayed tracked — an ignore rule does not untrack what git already follows.
bin/

# ADR-063: component descriptors are copied into the bundle chart at package
# time so a released cluster needs nothing outside the bundle to learn what its
# boundaries contain. The copy is a build artifact -- committing it would be a
# second declaration of what manifests/argocd/components/ already states, and
# the two would drift the way every other duplicated list here has.
manifests/argocd/environment-manager/descriptors/
soloz
# Scaffolded tenant repositories created during local testing. They are their own
# git repositories and belong to the tenant, not to the platform.
*-gitops/
# The local end-to-end workspace: scripts/dev/local-e2e.sh clones the tenant
# repository here. It is a separate repository with its own remote, and a
# `git add -A` in this checkout has swept one in before.
.local-e2e/
